abstract: >-
  Typst source and Python code of the monograph "A Cohn-tree reduction of the Frobenius–Markov uniqueness conjecture"
  (submitted, 2026), which reduces the uniqueness conjecture for Markov numbers to an exceptional terminal arithmetic
  theorem and proves that theorem in its minimal exceptional direction. Exact integer checks eliminate the seventeen
  one-parameter families left by the reductions, by congruences modulo 5, 23, 37 and 47 and a symbolic positivity
  margin; exploratory scripts test the conventions and expose false proof strategies. Everything runs with the Python
  standard library alone.
